.venv
.DS_Store
__pycache__
*.code-workspace
.git_corrupt_*
doc/refs/papers/*
# ...but the hand-written gist sidecars ARE tracked; only the copyrighted PDFs
# are ignored. (None checked in currently; gists live in doc/refs/GIST.md.)
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing comments — a comment after a pattern becomes
# part of the pattern and the rule silently never matches.
!doc/refs/papers/*.md
cache
doc/20250902_보안성검토(KSAS정현용_Pcd)
artifacts
target/
.cursor
.specstory
.vscode/settings.json
figures/debug/

# 연구노트 are a standalone project — each note directory is its own git repo.
doc/notes/

# paper renders (regenerate: tools/render_paper.py). The society's own template
# PDF is provenance, not a render, so it is exempt.
paper/**/*.pdf
!paper/**/template/*.pdf
paper/**/*.docx.tmp

# xelatex build droppings from tools/render_poster.py. poster.pdf itself is
# already covered by paper/**/*.pdf above -- it is a render, not a source.
paper/**/*.aux
paper/**/*.log
paper/**/*.out
paper/**/a0header.ps

# the poster's camera-picking viewer is generated and vendors plotly (6 MB):
# regenerate with paper/ksas_2026_fall/poster/lift_viewer.py
paper/**/lift_viewer.html

# poster previews and the view-picking viewer: both are regenerated on demand
# (make_poster_figures.py --png, lift_viewer.py) and the viewer vendors plotly.
paper/**/poster/*.png
paper/**/poster/lift_viewer.html
paper/**/a0header.ps

# scratch handoffs between sessions — not a record, use the repo for that
tmp/
tmp.md
